    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the personalized prevention plan updated, with a written copy given. Depression, cognitive, and fall-risk screens are negative. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left hand osteoarthritis (M19.042)</content>. Improving with exercise, the splint, topical diclofenac, and the injection in April. [S]<list><item>Continue the current plan; review next month as scheduled.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Gout (M1A.9XX0)</content>. No flare; urate 5.4 mg/dL in March. [S]<list><item>Serum urate at next month&apos;s review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bone health</content>. At 85, with low-normal weight and a fall-prone trade, a bone density test would change management. [S]<list><item>Order DXA of the hip and spine.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at his age; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Single dose two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 four years ago; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap given with the finger repair in June</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; ladder and studio safety reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>DXA ordered; the USPSTF finds the evidence insufficient for men, but at 85 with fall risk the result would guide treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended after 85</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm and lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended at 70 or older</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Glucose 92 mg/dL in March</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed; eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: High-dose influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis monograph (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: DXA in the next month. Hand and gout review with serum urate, kidney tests, and ALT next month. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-19: hand osteoarthritis and gout review at about seven months. [S]</paragraph></text>

